#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096440 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096643 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "48579a8d-61f0-50c1-81f6-7b087b3f936c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Magnitude of a Sum of Vectors Using the Pythagorean Theorem"}] :question/id #uuid "8cc1617d-ba3f-5ae3-aca0-90354ffbd62f" :question/math-academy-id "e-4273" :question/problem "The vector $\\mathbf{a}$ is directed due north-east and $\\mid \\mathbf{a}|=11$. The vector $\\mathbf{b}$ is directed due south-east and $\\mid \\mathbf{b}|=8$. Find the exact value of $\\mid \\mathbf{a}+\\textbf{b} \\mid$." :question/worked-solution "We use the triangle law of addition to find the sum $\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b}$:\n\n![](images/a1/a122c2a1146f27a089f991f7e0bd07e4180ca4622bfc95a6b85afc83f339c11d.png)\n\nNotice that we obtain a right triangle. So, we can use Pythagorean theorem as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{vmatrix}a + b & ^{2} &= & a & ^{2} +\\left.\\end{vmatrix}b\\right|^{2} \\\\\n&= 11^{2} + 8^{2} \\\\\n&= 185\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mid \\mathbf{a}+\\textbf{b} &= \\sqrt{185}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096442 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096645 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c145c97c-c313-597f-b84e-8adb3bdf9c14" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Magnitude of a Sum of Vectors Using the Law of Cosines"}] :question/id #uuid "f0c94cce-790d-50b0-bd9b-13b64867848b" :question/math-academy-id "e-4275" :question/problem "Consider the diagram shown above. If $\\mid \\mathbf{a}|=4$ and $\\mid \\mathbf{b}|=3$, Find the exact value of$\\mid \\mathbf{a-b} \\mid$.\n\n![](images/92/922fa6572855e2a40f2b0fdd97bbbc5d6ddf2323228d99d5ab74a7aa7c2072f8.png)" :question/worked-solution "We can interpret the subtraction\n$\\mid \\mathbf{a}-\\mathbf{b} \\mid$\nas the addition\n$\\mid \\mathbf{a} + (-\\mathbf{b}) \\mid$.\n\nThe vector $-\\mathbf{b}$ has the same magnitude as $\\mathbf{b}$ and the direction that is opposite to $\\mathbf{b}$. We use the triangle law of addition to find $\\mathbf{a}$ and $-\\mathbf{b}$. The resultant goes from the start of $\\mathbf{a}$ to the head of $-\\mathbf{b}$, as shown below.\n\n![](images/8b/8b1cd51e96439a8e3317fec12c9d1e57aa06bc9a99680849990e853d3ce6dbf7.png)\n\nSo, we can use the law of cosines as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{vmatrix}a - b & ^{2} &= \\end{vmatrix}a + \\left.(-b)\\right|^{2} \\\\\n&=\\begin{vmatrix}a & ^{2} + & -b & ^{2} - 2 \\cdot & a & \\cdot & -b\\end{vmatrix}\\cdot \\cos (180^{∘} - 120^{∘}) \\\\\n&=\\begin{vmatrix}a & ^{2} + & b & ^{2} - 2 & a\\end{vmatrix} \\mid b \\mid \\cos (60^{∘}) \\\\\n&= 3^{2} + 4^{2} - 2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 4 \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\\n&= 9 + 16 - 12 \\\\\n&= 13\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mid \\mathbf{a-b} &= \\sqrt{13}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096485 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096690 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e0146b8-421b-5d63-a933-3de9bcaa7ab2" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Magnitude of a Vector From a Diagram"}] :question/id #uuid "ba160db3-7799-5a25-8c50-5147100f7475" :question/math-academy-id "e-5013" :question/problem "Consider the picture shown below. Find the exact value of $\\mid \\mathbf{a} \\mid$.\n\n![](images/14/140b4f8ced622eaf505d97c0f4d9c029365536927ea0c3e38e76904cba84ace2.png)" :question/worked-solution "![](images/1f/1fc7b5efcaa81dd1a3416757c976e5d17b96f5040069b5eeeb941b1f7c149c34.png)\n\nIn $\\bigtriangleup AHB$ we have\n\n$$\n\\angle AHB = 90^\\circ\n$$\n\n,\n\n$$\nAH=35\\:\\textrm{mm}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\nBH=25\\:\\textrm{mm}\n$$\n\nSo, the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nAB &= \\sqrt{AH^{2} + BH^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{35^{2} + 25^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{1850} \\\\\n&= 5\\sqrt{74}mm\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572176 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096645 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c145c97c-c313-597f-b84e-8adb3bdf9c14" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Magnitude of a Sum of Vectors Using the Law of Cosines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12d2a9ec-fb95-5d20-a726-63f5771b10f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571570} {:answer/id #uuid "390cf7e7-f277-521d-acc2-2719c16d4347" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{31}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571641} {:answer/id #uuid "3f9d5909-94e6-5d98-bed0-36ed77f8c2ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571656} {:answer/id #uuid "845a2766-707b-53f6-be2f-35e563eda9f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{39}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571766} {:answer/id #uuid "9b9261ec-bdc7-547d-99c9-49c3876ad9c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{37}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571809}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b9261ec-bdc7-547d-99c9-49c3876ad9c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{37}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571809} :answer-field/id #uuid "b243cc54-a33f-576c-b54c-700231d1a2f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572065}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c6713e37-7e62-534f-9e1d-40cff7fc1ed3" :question/math-academy-id "q-11887" :question/problem "![](images/d1/d19c7802a136d6fd039c190acdda94e9e8603d58d2ba62864ea0e5522cbd6791.png)\n\nGiven the diagram above, where $|a|=3$ and $|b|=4$, find the value of $|a+b|.$" :question/worked-solution "We use the triangle law for adding the vectors $a$ and $b.$\n\n![](images/38/3858242481fec9cd3b3fef85fcbb4e6a17aff20128f47565807a253dba517585.png)\n\nUsing the law of cosines, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{|a+b|}^{2} & ={|a|}^{2}+{|b|}^{2}-2|a||b|\\operatorname{cos}⁡({120}^{∘}) \\\\  & ={3}^{2}+{4}^{2}-2\\cdot 3\\cdot 4\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =9+16+12 \\\\  & =37\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $|a+b|=\\sqrt{37}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572122 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096643 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "48579a8d-61f0-50c1-81f6-7b087b3f936c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Magnitude of a Sum of Vectors Using the Pythagorean Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27fb93c3-9d2f-5ad6-9943-7e3ee42dca71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571605} {:answer/id #uuid "45bfd978-6e30-5951-92eb-b82ea3ef3ad2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571663} {:answer/id #uuid "64501922-14f1-5b68-9bb8-4a18b9118b75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571710} {:answer/id #uuid "7983f355-aa20-5834-9494-e646a432ba66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571749} {:answer/id #uuid "99756e33-2341-5970-963d-037979ab31fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571805}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27fb93c3-9d2f-5ad6-9943-7e3ee42dca71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571605} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8fd3f51-46fc-5947-b8e0-a2f5fa5f7025" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572101}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "32c27023-4101-5727-960c-ccfbce16099a" :question/math-academy-id "q-118910" :question/problem "The vector $a$ is directed due west and $|a|=16.$ The vector $b$ is directed vertically up and $|b|=8.$ Find $|a+b|.$" :question/worked-solution "We use the triangle law of addition to add the vectors $a$ and $b.$\n\n![](images/b3/b3a60238ad44009f35ea661e39a2a5c60580f0b56149d0ad372ed52461b348c5.png)\n\nNotice that we obtain a right triangle. So, we can use Pythagorean theorem as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{|a+b|}^{2} & ={|a|}^{2}+{|b|}^{2} \\\\  & ={16}^{2}+{8}^{2} \\\\  & =320\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $|a+b|=\\sqrt{320}=8\\sqrt{5}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572123 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096690 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e0146b8-421b-5d63-a933-3de9bcaa7ab2" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Magnitude of a Vector From a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c263afd-03e6-5859-b1a5-42ab4791d10b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571752}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7c263afd-03e6-5859-b1a5-42ab4791d10b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571752} :answer-field/id #uuid "79a25629-7a8d-5411-bacd-30c7224e71e8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572037}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3ba76054-9f72-50d9-a7e8-25a2eccb8d81" :question/math-academy-id "q-275711" :question/problem "![](images/a2/a2efe530287edefcee1609c5765d84c9608c5680f80a056819692f80a2e8c0f9.png)\n\nConsider the picture shown above. Find the **exact** value of $|a+b|.$\n\n$|a+b|=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,\\text{mm}.$" :question/worked-solution "We use the triangle law of addition for $a$ and $b.$ We can start $a$ from an arbitrary point on the plane. The resultant goes from the start of $a$ to the head of $b.$\n\n![](images/41/41bd69400fe98c2f8ab964c76fa295a6624f83d51fc720ba251ae4c618f87954.png)\n\nNow, in $△AHB,$ we have $m∠AHB={90}^{∘},$ $AH=30\\,\\text{mm},$ and $BH=10\\,\\text{mm}.$ So, the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a+b| & =AB \\\\  & =\\sqrt{A{H}^{2}+B{H}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{30}^{2}+{10}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{900+100} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1000} \\\\  & =10\\sqrt{10}\\,\\text{mm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $|a+b|=10\\sqrt{10}\\,\\text{mm}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572112 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096643 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "48579a8d-61f0-50c1-81f6-7b087b3f936c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Magnitude of a Sum of Vectors Using the Pythagorean Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89edc1c1-7bea-5291-97c7-b99ff5980aa1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{34}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571776}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "89edc1c1-7bea-5291-97c7-b99ff5980aa1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{34}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571776} :answer-field/id #uuid "0843c3b9-ca94-5b83-889e-fb8a14d6ed3b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571987}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "17cfca30-50dc-5c14-8dd0-380912333363" :question/math-academy-id "q-316807" :question/problem "The vector $a$ is directed due west and $|a|=15.$ The vector $b$ is directed vertically up and $|b|=9.$ Find the **exact** value of $|a+b|.$\n\n$|a+b|=$\n {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the triangle law of addition to add the vectors $a$ and $b.$\n\n![](images/a4/a493346a118732d2b435e1757bcbabe756c5d0482aec0688c095b7151352d4c7.png)\n\nNotice that we obtain a right triangle. So, we can use the Pythagorean theorem as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{|a+b|}^{2} & ={|a|}^{2}+{|b|}^{2} \\\\  & ={15}^{2}+{9}^{2} \\\\  & =306\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $|a+b|=\\sqrt{306}=3\\sqrt{34}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572128 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096645 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c145c97c-c313-597f-b84e-8adb3bdf9c14" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Magnitude of a Sum of Vectors Using the Law of Cosines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e70770d-cb50-57ad-8704-19e1f2d7511b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{201}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571788}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e70770d-cb50-57ad-8704-19e1f2d7511b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{201}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571788} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2c77d03-16e4-5e98-9806-4ae53e282fdb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572067}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4a16473f-5565-58aa-afbf-78ab6b462353" :question/math-academy-id "q-317060" :question/problem "![](images/29/29e3f8ef81b98c4073e934a59f59557d399d105991c2386c3178c3840bd6ac3a.png)\n\nGiven the diagram above, where $|a|=5\\sqrt{3}$ and $|b|=6,$ find the **exact** value of $|a+b|.$\n\n$|a+b|=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the triangle law for adding the vectors $a$ and $b.$\n\n![](images/c5/c58fcaace0fd6b1161426357025da18aaccd182b7035db152221bdfddbe28226.png)\n\nUsing the law of cosines, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a+b{|}^{2} & =|a{|}^{2}+|b{|}^{2}-2|a||b|\\operatorname{cos}⁡{150}^{∘} \\\\  & =(5\\sqrt{3})^{2}+{6}^{2}-2\\cdot (5\\sqrt{3})\\cdot 6\\cdot \\,(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\  & =75+36+90 \\\\  & =201.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get\n\n$$\n|a+b|=\\sqrt{201}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572148 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096690 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e0146b8-421b-5d63-a933-3de9bcaa7ab2" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Magnitude of a Vector From a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23af22cb-5a66-56af-8a6e-a750ebfdd947" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{mm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571598} {:answer/id #uuid "3a4098af-5a86-5ee1-b39a-68dcdd7adfb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{15}\\,\\text{mm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571645} {:answer/id #uuid "473e76ef-59a4-58d5-ac39-765fc9788603" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{mm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571665} {:answer/id #uuid "bd3db554-af50-52f9-9ed6-d8cd7fc6d102" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{61}\\,\\text{mm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571876} {:answer/id #uuid "df1422f1-6572-5a6f-9f13-2c4031c88aee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25\\,\\text{mm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571937}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd3db554-af50-52f9-9ed6-d8cd7fc6d102" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{61}\\,\\text{mm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571876} :answer-field/id #uuid "999d96da-ead9-58f1-95d7-05e3fcaf8038" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572051}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "802cdf34-1293-5319-b775-69d99d9605a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-69501" :question/problem "![](images/d3/d32ceace77d77dc5a3b9b1443b0985232ac23837a5cb5b2b5c6969e7cc65bfef.png)\n\nConsider the picture shown above. Find $|a|.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/f2/f2144a9accce690363d34c31ed1c29b4742281eb26c273c91a55776c0ad54e5a.png)\n\nIn $△AHB$ we have $∠AHB={90}^{∘}$, $AH=30\\,\\text{mm}$ and $BH=25\\,\\text{mm}.$ So, the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\sqrt{A{H}^{2}+B{H}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{30}^{2}+{25}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1\\,525} \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{61}\\,\\text{mm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
